  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.24,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.15,
    "rationale": "The plateau at ~1.21–1.26 could have been caused by the reader saturating, so I diluted late-time aliquots to bring them into the low-OD range and corrected for the dilution. 18 h at 10x gave 0.1325 and 0.1375, which corrects to ~1.35. 18 h at 20x gave 0.0589 and 0.0573, which corrects to ~1.16. Together these bracket the undiluted reading of 1.209 (mean ~1.25). 15 h at 10x gave 0.1265, which corrects to 1.265, matching the undiluted 1.261. As a check at low OD, 4 h at 10x gave 0.0373, which corrects to 0.373 against 0.408 undiluted. That suggests about ±10% error from diluting and pipetting, and no sign that diluted readings come out systematically higher. If the reader were saturated, the diluted, corrected values would sit well above the plateau, and they don't. The 10x and 20x results also disagree in direction, so there's no consistent pattern. The plateau looks like real stationary phase at OD ~1.2–1.25, not an artefact of the reader. The 18 h estimate (~1.24) is the average of the undiluted and dilution-corrected values."
  },
